<title>SPAIN: Spain motorway tolls to fall 8 pct from Sept - Costa.</title>
<headline>Spain motorway tolls to fall 8 pct from Sept - Costa.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish motorway tolls are to fall around eight percent from September 1, 1997, Secretary of State for the Exchequer Juan Costa told a parliamentary committee on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the Exchequer told Reuters that the government has to negotiate with the European Commission on how it will compensate motorway firms for the reduction in toll income.</p>
<p>If Brussels approves the move, the government can cut the value-added tax rate the firms pay to seven percent from the present 16 percent. If not, the government will study alternative methods of compensation, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
